From 9c3d65dcc31d8a9390e8b605db676e1c3b532144 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:52:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 267/267] media: amlogic: amvdec: add AV1 decoding on S4

Add stateless AV1 (Main profile, 8 and 10-bit, up to 4096x2304) decoding
on the S4 HEVC core with the secure-world AV1 MMU firmware.

The firmware parses the bitstream itself. Rebuild a sequence header and
a frame OBU for each request from the controls, using explicit sizes,
reference indices, tile sizes and full segmentation and loop filter data
so that no decoder history is needed, and feed them with the Amlogic
framing. Program the reference slot table before the frame is parsed,
and the reference, motion field projection, loop filter, CDEF, upscale,
CDF and segment map state at the frame header, from the controls and
from state kept for each CAPTURE buffer. Film grain is not applied.

The firmware signals on HEVC mailbox 0, so request that interrupt when
the DT has it. Load the non-swap firmware, which takes the CDF write
address in SCRATCH_8, and keep the unused second write paths disabled.

Decode to NV12M, or to AM21C compressed frames for 8 and 10-bit
streams, with the FBC buffers sized from the sequence bit depth.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
